<title>USA: Thoratec gets OK in Japan for graft.</title>
<headline>Thoratec gets OK in Japan for graft.</headline>
<dateline>BERKELEY, Calif. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thoratec Laboratories Corp said Monday it received approval from the Japanese Ministry of Health to begin marketing its vascular access graft (VAG) in that country.</p>
<p>Shares of Thoratec gained 1-3/8 to 7-1/8.</p>
<p>The VAG, currently available in several countries including Canada and Australia, is used for patients undergoing renal dialysis.  Thoratec said it plans to begin marketing this product through its exclusive distributor, Goodman Company Ltd.</p>
<p>Thoratec Laboratories develops and manufactures medical devices for circulatory support and vascular graft applications.</p>
</text>
